            "review_title": "Review at Xưởng Bia Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Rob Nesbit\nWarsaw, Poland6958 contributions\n1\nStrongly recommended!\nApr 2023\nHad their signature beers, Cong Xuong One and Two, The Jasmine IPA and the Imperial Stout.\nThe beers were great, very tasty, loved them.\n\nI was sad to see the Stout was a Heart of Darkness stout, I had no idea HOD meant that. That company refused entry to some Vietnamese people into their establishment during Covid so this leaves a bitter taste for sure in my mouth and hence will refuse to give them the time of day ever since. Not exactly in the spirit of Conrad! So duck them. ok rant over!\n\nThe dish we ordered was beef with gravy, and a baked potato and some veg. It was great, the beef was delicious and the gravy was to die for...….lovely presentation and well cooked. Hats off to the chef.\n\nNice atmosphere and a lot of space\nStaff were very friendly and efficient.\n\nThe menu looked great, a good mix of Vietnamese and Western dishes, and the beer list looks enticing. The price as far as I can remember was affordable too.\nIf I'm around again in the future, I WILL be back\n\nStrongly recommended!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 4, 2023",
